---
/**
 * C-6 · Completion / confirmation — `CONTACT_WIREFRAME.md` C-6 (Page IA Stage E).
 * Component (Inventory): **Confirmation Message** · CTA Group (optional, light).
 *
 * Responsibility realized: "confirm receipt and that the enquiry reached the
 * right context; close the loop without scattering the visitor."
 *
 * Spatial composition, transcribed: "a clean confirmation that echoes the
 * context — *'Your enquiry about [Service] has been received.'* **Avoid forced
 * onward navigation:** the goal was reached; any return links are optional and
 * quiet. **Calm closure, not a new funnel.**"
 *
 * ── ONE STATE OF ONE PAGE, NOT A SECOND URL ────────────────────────────────
 * `CONTACT_PAGE_IA.md` C-6 makes confirmation a state ("submission → one inbox"
 * → "confirmation"), not a route. A `/contact/multumim` page would be a URL the
 * frozen route map (§11.1) does not have, and it would let a visitor land on a
 * receipt for an enquiry they never sent. So the confirmation ships hidden
 * beside the form and the island swaps them.
 *
 * ── IT IS SHOWN FOR EXACTLY ONE OUTCOME ────────────────────────────────────
 * `enquiry.ts` classifies a submission as `sent` | `failed` | `unavailable`, and
 * only `sent` reaches this module. In particular the pre-Phase-7 `unavailable`
 * state — the endpoint does not exist yet — never renders a confirmation, which
 * is the single most important thing this page must not get wrong.
 *
 * ── FOCUS AND ANNOUNCEMENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `tabindex="-1"` so the island can move focus here when the form it replaces
 * disappears (WCAG 2.2 AA 2.4.3 — focus must not be lost to `document.body`),
 * and the heading is what gets announced on arrival. The region is `hidden`
 * until then, so nothing about it is perceivable — or reachable by keyboard —
 * while the form is still the page.
 *
 * The one onward link is the Homepage, quiet and optional, exactly as the
 * wireframe qualifies it. No hub link is added: the visitor's pillar is known
 * only when a prefill carried it, and offering a different destination depending
 * on how someone arrived at a completed conversation is the scattering C-6
 * forbids.
 */
import type { Locale } from '../../lib/content';
import type { ContactMessages } from '../../lib/i18n/contact';
import { routePath } from '../../lib/i18n/routes';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
  copy: ContactMessages['confirmation'];
}

const { locale, copy } = Astro.props;
---

<section
  class="c-confirm"
  id="c-confirmation"
  aria-labelledby="c-confirm-heading"
  tabindex="-1"
  data-confirmation
  hidden
>
  <h2 class="c-confirm-heading" id="c-confirm-heading">{copy.heading}</h2>

  {/* The three receipt shapes: plain, pillar-echoing, service-echoing. The
      island picks one from the RESOLVED prefill and fills it with authored
      labels — never with the query string (§23.1). */}
  <p
    class="c-confirm-body"
    data-confirmation-body
    data-plain={copy.body}
    data-topic={copy.bodyTopic}
    data-service={copy.bodyService}
  >
    {copy.body}
  </p>

  <p class="c-confirm-onward">
    <a href={routePath('home', locale)}>
      {copy.home}
      <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </p>
</section>
